:question
$()Soit la fonction 
!insmath f
$() définie sur $val19 par <span class="nowrap">
!insmath f(x)= $val28
$().</span>	<div class="wims_question"><ol>	<li><label for="reply1">Donner l'expression de </label> <span class="nowrap">
!insmath f'(x)
$() :  
!read oef/embed.phtml reply1,20 
$()</span>.</li>	<li><label for="reply2">Puis calculer </label> <span class="nowrap">
!insmath f'($val18)
$() :  
!read oef/embed.phtml reply2 
$()</span>	<br><label for="reply3">et </label><span class="nowrap">
!insmath f($val18)
$() : 
!read oef/embed.phtml reply3 
$().</span></li>	<li><label for="reply4">Enfin donner une valeur approchée au millième de </label><span class="nowrap">
!insmath f($val31)
$() :	 
!read oef/embed.phtml reply4 
$()</span>.</li>					</ol>	</div>	
$()
!exit

:hint
$()Une valeur approchée par approximation affine s'obtient par&nbsp;:	<div class="wimscenter unbreakable">
!insmath f(x_0+h) \simeq f(x_0)+f'(x_0)h
$().</div>
$()
!exit

:help
$()
$()
!exit

:solution
$()	<ul class="wims_nopuce">	<li>On sait que&nbsp;:<br> <div class="wims_scrollable">
!insmath f($val31) \simeq f($val18) + f'($val18)($val31-$val35)
$()</div></li>	<li>Or : <br>	<div class="wims_scrollable">
!insmath f($val18) + f'($val18)($val31-$val35) = $val30 + $val36 \times $val37
$()<br>	
!insmath \phantom{  f($val18) + f'($val18)($val31-$val35)}= $val34 
$()	</div></li>	</ul>	Conclusion&nbsp;: 
!insmath f($val31) \simeq $val34 
$()
$()
!exit

